You are all set to launch and test your emulator right now:

1. Cold Boot Your Pixel 5

• Open Android Studio: Click the Android Studio icon on your left dock.
• Cold Boot: In Device Manager, click the three vertical dots (⋮) next to Pixel 5 and select Cold Boot Now so your new SerialConsole = off setting takes effect.

2. Connect AndroidWifi to Burp Suite

• Turn Wi-Fi ON: Once the phone boots up, swipe down from the top bar and tap the Wi-Fi icon to turn on AndroidWifi.
• Confirm Manual Proxy: On AndroidWifi, tap the gear icon > pencil icon (Edit) > Advanced options, and make sure Proxy is set to Manual with Proxy hostname: 10.0.2.2 and Proxy port: 8080.
• Check Burp Listener: Make sure Burp Suite is open on your laptop with its proxy listener on port 8080 running and bound to All interfaces.

3. Test Interception

• Open Chrome inside the emulator and visit http://burpsuite or https://example.com.
• Check Burp Suite: Look at Proxy > HTTP history to confirm traffic is flowing cleanly, then turn Intercept is on whenever you are ready to inspect packets.
